  <section id="wissenai-identify-package">
<h1>wissenai.identify package<a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai-identify-package" title="Link to this heading"></a></h1>
<section id="submodules">
<h2>Submodules<a class="headerlink" href="#submodules" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
</section>
<section id="module-wissenai.identify.layout_detection">
<span id="wissenai-identify-layout-detection-module"></span><h2>wissenai.identify.layout_detection module<a class="headerlink" href="#module-wissenai.identify.layout_detection" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.convert_numpy">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">convert_numpy</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">data</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#convert_numpy"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.convert_numpy" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Recursively converts numpy types to native Python types for JSON serialization.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>data: Input data which may contain numpy types (ndarray, integer, floating).</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>The converted data with all numpy types replaced by native Python types.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.convert_pdf_to_images">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">convert_pdf_to_images</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">batch_size</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">20</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">150</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#convert_pdf_to_images"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.convert_pdf_to_images" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Converts a PDF file to a series of images.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the PDF file.
batch_size (int): Number of pages to process at once.
dpi (int): DPI (dots per inch) for the output images.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>generator: A generator that yields batches of PIL Image objects.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.dict_to_dataframe">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">dict_to_dataframe</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">data</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#dict_to_dataframe"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.dict_to_dataframe" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Convert a dictionary with lists of varying lengths into a DataFrame with dynamic column names.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Parameters:</dt><dd><p>data (dict): A dictionary where each key corresponds to a row in the DataFrame, and the value is a list of column values.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>pd.DataFrame: A DataFrame with dynamically generated column names.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.enhance_dpi">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">enhance_dpi</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">image</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">new_dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">300</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">old_dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">150</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#enhance_dpi"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.enhance_dpi" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Enhances the DPI of an image by resizing it.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>image (PIL.Image): Input image.
new_dpi (int): Desired output DPI.
old_dpi (int): Original DPI of the image.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>PIL.Image: The resized image with enhanced DPI.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.extract_text_from_bbox">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">extract_text_from_bbox</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">image</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">bbox</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#extract_text_from_bbox"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.extract_text_from_bbox" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Extracts text from a specified bounding box in an image.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>image (PIL.Image or np.ndarray): Input image.
bbox (dict): Bounding box coordinates with keys ‘xmin’, ‘ymin’, ‘xmax’, ‘ymax’.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>str: The extracted text from the bounding box region.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Raises:</dt><dd><p>TypeError: If the input image type is not supported.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_and_sort_headers">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">filter_and_sort_headers</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">data</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">modified_json_output_filepath</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#filter_and_sort_headers"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_and_sort_headers" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Filters and sorts header blocks (Page-header and Section-header) from layout data.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>data (dict): The input layout data.
modified_json_output_filepath (str): Path to save the modified JSON output.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>tuple: (sorted_data, modified_json_output_filepath) where sorted_data is the filtered and sorted data.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_and_sort_layouts">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">filter_and_sort_layouts</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">data</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">modified_json_output_filepath</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#filter_and_sort_layouts"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_and_sort_layouts" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Filters and sorts layout blocks from the input data.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>data (dict): The input layout data.
modified_json_output_filepath (str): Path to save the modified JSON output.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>tuple: (sorted_layout_data, modified_json_output_filepath) where sorted_layout_data is the filtered and sorted data.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_layout_blocks">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">filter_layout_blocks</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">input_data</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#filter_layout_blocks"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.filter_layout_blocks" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Filters the blocks with label_name ‘Table’ from the input data.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>input_data (dict): The input JSON data.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>list: A list containing only the blocks with label_name ‘Table’.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.get_file_name_without_extension">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">get_file_name_without_extension</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#get_file_name_without_extension"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.get_file_name_without_extension" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Extracts the file name without its extension from a given file path.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): The full path to the file.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>str: The file name without the extension.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.layout_detection">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">layout_detection</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">img_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">model=YOLOv10</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#layout_detection"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.layout_detection" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Performs layout detection on an image using YOLOv10 model.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>img_path (str): Path to the input image.
model: The YOLOv10 model to use for detection.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>tuple: (annotated_image, detections, results) where:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>annotated_image: The input image with detection annotations</p></li>
<li><p>detections: The detection results</p></li>
<li><p>results: Raw model results</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.layout_pipeline">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">layout_pipeline</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">None</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">label_name</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">None</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">directory_path</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">None</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#layout_pipeline"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.layout_pipeline" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Main pipeline for processing PDF or image files to extract layout information.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the input file (PDF or image).
label_name (str, optional): Specific label to filter (e.g., ‘Table’).
directory_path (str): Directory to store output files.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>tuple: Depending on input parameters, returns various combinations of:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>sorted_layout_data: Processed layout data</p></li>
<li><p>class_names: Model class names</p></li>
<li><p>table_excel_dir: Directory containing Excel tables</p></li>
<li><p>bbox_images_path: Directory containing images with bounding boxes</p></li>
<li><p>cropped_images_path: Directory containing cropped images (if label_name specified)</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
<dt>Note:</dt><dd><p>For PDF inputs, processes pages in batches.
For image inputs, processes single image.
Creates multiple output directories for different types of output.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.read_json">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">read_json</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">json_file</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#read_json"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.read_json" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd></dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.save_cropped_image">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">save_cropped_image</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">cropped_image</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">save_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#save_cropped_image"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.save_cropped_image" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Save cropped images to the specified path.</p>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.save_table_to_excel">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">save_table_to_excel</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">extracted_text</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">table_excel_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">table_id</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">page_number</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#save_table_to_excel"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.save_table_to_excel" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd></dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.identify.layout_detection.tsr_inference_image">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.identify.layout_detection.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">tsr_inference_image</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">image</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/identify/layout_detection.html#tsr_inference_image"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.identify.layout_detection.tsr_inference_image" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Performs table structure recognition (TSR) on an input image.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>image (str or PIL.Image): Either a path to an image file or a PIL Image object.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>pd.DataFrame: A DataFrame containing the extracted table data.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Note:</dt><dd><p>The function measures and prints the time taken for table extraction.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

</section>
